# Beitco  -  Cursor Rules
# This file configures Cursor AI for this project.

You are working on **Beitco**, an Egyptian real estate social network.

## Quick Context
- Read `.ai/ENTRY_PROMPT.md` for full project context
- Read `.ai/TASKS.md` for current task board
- Read `.ai/CURRENT_STATE.md` for what's built vs not

## Tech Stack (Non-Negotiable)
- Backend: NestJS 11 + TypeScript 5.x + Prisma ORM + PostgreSQL 16 + PostGIS
- Frontend: Next.js 15 (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- Mobile: Capacitor 6.x (wraps Next.js → iOS App Store + Google Play)
- Video: Mux (HLS streaming)
- Search: Meilisearch
- Cache: Redis (Upstash in prod)
- Jobs: BullMQ
- Payments: Paymob (Egyptian methods)
- Monorepo: Turborepo + pnpm

## Coding Rules
1. TypeScript strict mode  -  no `any`, no `as` casts, no `@ts-ignore`
2. All API responses use `ApiResponse<T>` wrapper: `{ success, data, meta?, error? }`
3. UUID primary keys, `snake_case` DB columns, `camelCase` TypeScript
4. Soft deletes with `deleted_at` column
5. Arabic is the primary language  -  RTL is the default direction
6. All user-facing strings must be in both Arabic and English
7. Permission checks use `@RequireTier(X)` decorator
8. Cursor-based pagination everywhere (no offset)
9. NestJS: one module per feature, services inject PrismaService
10. Frontend: Server Components by default, 'use client' only when needed
11. Use logical CSS properties (`margin-inline-start`, not `margin-left`)

## File Organization
```
apps/api/src/{module}/
├── {module}.module.ts
├── {module}.controller.ts
├── {module}.service.ts
├── {module}.service.spec.ts
└── dto/
    ├── create-{module}.dto.ts
    └── update-{module}.dto.ts

apps/web/src/
├── app/[locale]/(app)/     # authenticated pages
├── app/[locale]/(auth)/    # login, register
├── app/[locale]/(admin)/   # admin panel (Tier 1)
├── components/{feature}/   # feature components
├── components/ui/          # shadcn primitives
├── hooks/                  # custom hooks
├── lib/                    # utilities, API client, capacitor helpers
└── i18n/                   # ar.json, en.json

apps/web/
├── ios/                    # Capacitor iOS shell (auto-generated)
├── android/                # Capacitor Android shell (auto-generated)
└── capacitor.config.ts     # Capacitor config
```

## Capacitor Rules
- ALWAYS provide web fallbacks for native features
- Use `Capacitor.isNativePlatform()` for platform detection
- Dynamic import Capacitor plugins  -  never at module top level
- Test on web, iOS Simulator, and Android Emulator

## Key Patterns
- NestJS guards: `JwtAuthGuard` for auth, `TierGuard` for tier checks
- Error format: `throw new ForbiddenException({ code: 'TIER_REQUIRED', message: '...' })`
- Post creation: Tier 2 auto-publishes, Tier 3 goes to approval queue
- Feed: 3 tabs (For You = algorithmic, Following = chronological, Videos = watch-time)

